; partycreation.eval - a CREATED party survives a save and a load
; (docs/party-creation-plan.md, phase 1).
;
; Run:  Dungeon.exe -headless -eval <path to this file>, then read dungeon.log.
; What it should show:
;   - the default four (`roster`), human, premade stats;
;   - `newparty` makes two members: Aria (elf: stats 9,14,8,13,11 - the race's
;     STR -1 DEX +2 VIT -2 INT +1, then DEX +2 and WIL +3 spent) and Old Tom
;     (dwarf: 13,9,15,10,9), each with two skills at level 2 and two starting items
;     where they belong (a weapon in a hand, armour on the body, food in the
;     pack), their own colours and faces;
;   - a reset puts the default four back;
;   - loading the save brings the two back exactly as `roster` first printed
;     them - names, races, colours, pace, stats, bases, skills and kit.
; (A refused spec - a bad race, too many points - fails a run, so those are
; checked by hand, not here.)

logecho on
reset
roster

newparty name=Aria race=elf portrait=portrait135 color=c04040 points=0,2,0,3,0 skills=blade,conditioning items=dagger,apple | name=Old_Tom race=dwarf portrait=b045 color=40a0c0 points=2,0,3,0,0 skills=blunt,heavy_armor items=club,padded_jack
roster
party
save eval_party

reset
roster

load eval_party
roster
party
